      "explanation": "Fritz Lang (Friedrich Christian Anton Lang - 1890–1976 - Vienna, Berlin & Hollywood) and the founding of modernist world cinema:\n- **Fritz Lang (Master of German Expressionism & Sci-Fi)**:\n  - Architect, visual visionary, and master director of Weimar Germany (UFA Studios Babelsberg); fled Nazi Germany in 1933 after rejecting Joseph Goebbels' offer to head the Reich film industry.\n- Monumental Masterpieces & Cinematic Inventions:\n  - **Metropolis (1927 - Inscribed in UNESCO's Memory of the World Register)**:\n    - The undisputed mother of all science fiction cinema (inspiring *Blade Runner*, *Star Wars*, and *The Matrix*);\n    - Depicts a hyper-stratified 2026 vertical megacity: wealthy oligarchs live in pleasure gardens atop colossal skyscrapers while underground workers toil like cogs inside colossal industrial machines (the Moloch);\n    - Features the robotic gynoid **Maschinenmensch Maria** constructed by inventor Rotwang;\n    - Crowned by the immortal guiding moral theorem: **«Mittler zwischen Hirn und Händen muss das Herz sein!»** (*\"The mediator between the head and the hands must be the heart!\"*);\n  - **M – Eine Stadt sucht einen Mörder (M - 1931 - Starring Peter Lorre as Hans Beckert)**:\n    - The supreme masterpiece of early psychological sound cinema;\n    - **Invention of the Sound Leitmotif (Akustisches Leitmotiv)**: The serial killer is identified by his compulsive, eerie off-screen whistling of Edvard Grieg's *In the Hall of the Mountain King*;\n    - Parallel manhunt where the police and the underworld criminal syndicate simultaneously track the killer across Berlin.",
